# =============================================================================
# Lumina Linux — Live ISO package list (x86_64)
# =============================================================================
# Consumed by `mkarchiso` to build the live environment.
#
# v0.1.8 RATIONALE — why this list shrank from ~200 → ~110 packages:
#   Lumina is supposed to be a LIGHTWEIGHT distro (<=100MB RAM idle). The
#   v0.1.7 list violated that goal by shipping gimp, inkscape, libreoffice,
#   steam, wine, multiple dev toolchains (rust/go/nodejs/npm/yarn/ruby/perl/
#   cmake/meson/vala), telegram-desktop, discord, etc. — adding ~2GB to the
#   ISO and dozens of background services on idle.
#
#   Trimmed to: base system + kernel + networking + XFCE core + browser +
#   basic media + Win11 theming + installer. Heavy apps (office suite,
#   image editors, games, dev tools) are installable on first boot via the
#   Pamac app store — that's what an app store is for.
#
# FORMATTING RULES (do not break these — every previous "target not found"
# error in v0.1.0-v0.1.7 traces back to one of these):
#   1. NO inline comments. A line like `mtools  # FAT tools` will be parsed
#      as `mtools  ` (with trailing whitespace) by mkarchiso's tokenizer and
#      pacman will report "target not found: mtools" even though the package
#      exists. Use full-line comments only.
#   2. NO version pins (pacstrap resolves from latest DB).
#   3. NO duplicates across this file and build-aur-packages.sh — a package
#      in both places causes pacstrap to fail with "duplicate target".
# =============================================================================

# ---------- Base system ----------
base
base-devel
linux
linux-headers
linux-firmware
linux-firmware-broadcom
linux-firmware-marvell
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
